==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|haust|lang=non}} from earlier {{term|haustr}} (masculine). Compare Old English {{term|hærfest}}, English {{term|harvest}}, the Old High German {{term|Herbist}}; German {{term|Herbst}}, Danish {{term|høst|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|höst|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/høyst/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|øyst|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n}}

# [[autumn]], [[fall]]
#: ''Ég úrskrifaðist '''haustið''' 2007.''
#:: I graduated '''fall''' 2007.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|h|au|st}}

====Derived terms====
* [[haustönn]]

